{"name":"Tortilla","hex":"#efdba7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tortilla","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of Mexican flatbread made out of cornmeal or flour.","Spanish omelette; a type of omelette containing potatoes and onions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tortilla"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tortilla","blocks":[{"text":"A tortilla is a thin, circular unleavened flatbread, originally made from corn (maize) but now also made of wheat flour. The corn tortilla is a staple food in most of Mexico and Central America, while the flour tortilla is typical of Northern Mexican and Mexican-American cuisine. The tortilla has become popular across the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Stacks_of_corn_tortillas_and_flour_tortillas%2C_with_the_top_one_rolled%2C_side_view_%282%29.jpg/330px-Stacks_of_corn_tortillas_and_flour_tortillas%2C_with_the_top_one_rolled%2C_side_view_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tortilla"},{"title":"Tortilla (restaurant chain)","blocks":[{"text":"Tortilla Mexican Grill PLC is a fast-food restaurant based in the United Kingdom, founded in 2007 by Brandon and Jennifer Stephens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Tortilla_-_Broad_Street_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6895869_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Tortilla_-_Broad_Street_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6895869_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tortilla_(restaurant_chain)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mexican_tortilla.jpg/500px-Mexican_tortilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mexican_tortilla.jpg/1280px-Mexican_tortilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars